tests:
  unit: { count: 367, covers: "Every rule at the level where it lives. THE CORE ENTRY (W1): flag parsing, the ready-line format, the stale-bundle check, the app's --core arguments, the dev argument passthrough. THE SUPERVISOR (W2, W3): attach-mode selection, the conflict sentence and the restart refusal, the log ring's bound, order and sequence, one start mark per spawned pid, a failed spawn published as exited, a core's late lines kept above the next start mark, the page's 2000-line cap pinned to the ring's, CA-dir resolution and ./ca adoption, fixed vs ephemeral ports, who hands over to a running instance. THE SHELL (W3): the Settings menu action, only main ends the app, the page mark pinned to page.ts. THE PAGE (W3): each core state's rendering, the restart warning (focus, Esc, closes once the core is no longer running), the attached variant, the log tail's bound and auto-scroll, NotAnswering's restart over an owned exited core, the snapshot read only after the listener registers. THE QUIT (W4): quitStopsCore per state, the owned and kept sentences per dialog case. THE E2E LAUNCHER (W5): two suites green only together, each tally named." }
  integration: { count: 18, covers: "Each WU's bounded contract. core_entry.rs (W1): the core entry on port 0 prints a parseable ready line, the API answers at it, stdin EOF exits with both ports rebindable. xtask/tests/ui.rs (W1): the trawler package links no tauri/wry/tao, the app links the core, both shell builds register exactly the commands the app invokes. supervisor.rs (W2, W3): kill -> exited(signal 9) -> restart on the same ports -> stop frees them; a SIGKILLed supervisor leaves no core; a held port is Conflict{port}; concurrent restarts run one after the other; one start mark per core. restart_command.rs (W3): restart round-trips through the supervisor over Tauri's mock runtime, attached refuses, Settings opens once and off the calling thread. quit_stops_core.rs (W4): RunEvent::Exit stops an owned core and frees its ports, and leaves an attached core running." }
  e2e: { count: 7, covers: "THE EPIC'S FULL FLOW through the real Tauri window (W5): cargo xtask ui e2e green over both suites, 8 of 8 attached spec files and 1 of 1 owned. one-app.spec.ts launches the app binary alone with no harness core: J1 the core is the app's child on ephemeral ports and a request through its proxy appears as a row and in GET /flows; J2 Settings shows the reported pid, ports and a start mark, a SIGKILL reads killed (signal 9) with the window alive, Restart gives a new pid on the same ports and a second start mark; J3 destroying the main window ends the app and its core and both ports bind. service-attached.spec.ts (J4) proves attach mode is real: the page reads attached, the harness's address, no log, no restart, beside the seven unchanged attached specs. The port-conflict dialog, single-instance focus and the parent-SIGKILL lifeline are native and proven at integration level." }
